.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-onboardings-correct - Correct a request's name, email or address and send a new link (write mode, audited)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin onboardings correct  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Replace the name, the email and/or the wallet address of a request that is not
completed, and send a new link to its email, saying what changed. The previous link stops
working, nothing goes to the address that was replaced, and an expired request is
renewed. At least one of --name / --email / --address, with a value that differs.

.PP
The same checks as an invite run on the result. A completed request is history (422
onboarding_completed): its account is corrected with 'rail0 account update --account'.

.PP
A write: it needs write mode ('rail0 admin write-mode on').


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--address\fP=""
	The corrected wallet address (0x…40 hex, or @alias)

.PP
\fB--email\fP=""
	The corrected contact email

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for correct

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	The corrected account name


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin onboardings correct 019f0c11-… --email right@acme.example
  rail0 admin onboardings correct 019f0c11-… --address 0x9F3A… --name "Acme Store Ltd"
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin-onboardings(1)\fP
